# Engine files that include a shell header.
#
# types.h -> tune.h is DELIBERATE: the include sits after types.h's own #endif
# so the SPSA macros reach anywhere types.h does, and removing it would make
# every future tuning run add an include first.
#
# The other two are engine code printing, and they are new only in the sense
# that they became VISIBLE: sync_cout and dbg_print used to live in misc.h, a
# platform file, so an engine file calling them produced an engine-to-platform
# edge that the shell check could not see. Moving the console half to
# shell/console.h put them where the rule can read them. They are the output
# sink seam B7 describes and does not build.
network.cpp -> console.h
search.cpp -> console.h
types.h -> tune.h
